  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations for Testing Laboratories (NAICS 541380) stood at $353M in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 38.5% year over year. Agencies made 2,634 awards so far, with an average award size of $134K. Annual obligations rose from $502M in FY21 to $671M in FY24, then declined to $574M in FY25 and to $353M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $165M in FY2026 to date, followed by several civilian agencies. The vendor list for FY2026 to date is led by AGILE DEFENSE, LLC at $29.2M, with MERRICK & COMPANY and RAYTHEON COMPANY also among the top suppliers. This market profile reflects a mid‑six‑figure average award and a concentrated buyer base, with defense and health agencies prominent among the top purchasers. Fiscal year totals for recent years show a peak in FY24 and a notable pullback through FY25 into FY26 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has spending changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 38.5% year over year, from $574M in FY25 to $353M in FY26 to date. After rising from $502M in FY21 to $671M in FY24, the market contracted through FY25 and into FY26 to date. The number of awards in FY2026 to date is 2,634 and the average award size is $134K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who dominates buying and selling in this NAICS?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $165M in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $44.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $31M. The top vendors in FY2026 to date include AGILE DEFENSE, LLC at $29.2M, MERRICK & COMPANY at $25.2M, and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $21.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
